# Minimal exec_type stubs for vendor binaries labeled in file_contexts that aren't
# declared anywhere in AOSP base sepolicy or device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr - mostly
# vivo/BBK-custom HAL services (vendor.vivo.hardware.*) and a handful of MTK-internal
# tools not covered by the common MTK policy. Declared here just enough to let the
# sepolicy compile (file_contexts referencing an undeclared type is a hard build
# error, independent of the androidboot.selinux=permissive runtime mode already set
# in BOARD_KERNEL_CMDLINE). Proper domains (hal_attribute_hwservice, init_daemon_domain,
# specific allow rules) should replace these stubs once real avc denials from an
# actual boot are available to drive them - see sepolicy/README-todo.md.

type vivo-fingerprint-sh_exec, exec_type, vendor_file_type, file_type;
